problem:
Problem description
- There are $$P$$ products indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ and a finite sequence of planning periods indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T}^{\mathrm{plan}}$$.
- For each product and period, the required market demand is given by $$d_{p,t}$$.
- For each product and period, the unit production cost is given by $$c_{p,t}$$.
- Each product has a unit storage volume $$v_p$$ measured in cubic meters per unit.
- The factory has a combined production capacity $$K_t$$ in each period for all products together.
- The factory has an in-house warehouse with volumetric capacity $$W$$.
- The in-house warehouse has a per-cubic-meter holding cost $$h_t^{\mathrm{own}}$$ in each period.
- External warehouse space may be rented whenever needed, with per-cubic-meter holding cost $$h_t^{\mathrm{ext}}$$ in each period.
- The initial inventory at the start of the first planning period is given by $$I_{p,0}$$ for each product.
- The planning goal is to determine a production and storage schedule over $$\mathcal{T}^{\mathrm{plan}}$$ that minimizes total production cost and total inventory holding cost while meeting all demand.

- Required business constraints:
  - Demand for every product in every planning period must be fully satisfied.
  - No shortage and no backlogging are allowed.
  - Production in any period, summed across all products, must not exceed the factory’s available combined capacity.
  - Inventory must be carried consistently from one period to the next.
  - The total inventory stored in the factory’s own warehouse in any period must not exceed its volumetric capacity.
  - Any inventory that does not fit in the factory warehouse may be placed in external storage, which is available as supplementary space and incurs a higher cost.
  - Inventory space usage must respect each product’s unit volume.
  - The initial inventory at the beginning of the first planning period is fixed and known.

- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$, the quantity of product $$p$$ produced in period $$t$$.
  - $$i_{p,t}^{\mathrm{own}}$$, the quantity of product $$p$$ held in the factory warehouse at the end of period $$t$$.
  - $$i_{p,t}^{\mathrm{ext}}$$, the quantity of product $$p$$ held in external storage at the end of period $$t$$.
  - $$\mathrm{TC}$$, the total cost of the plan.

Input Format
{
  "products": {
    "count": "$$P$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$"
  },
  "periods": {
    "count": "$$T$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{T}^{\\mathrm{plan}}$$",
    "description": "Ordered planning periods over which production and inventory are decided"
  },
  "demand": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "entry": "$$d_{p,t}$$",
    "description": "Demand of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$"
  },
  "production_cost": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "entry": "$$c_{p,t}$$",
    "description": "Unit production cost of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$"
  },
  "unit_volume": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "entry": "$$v_p$$",
    "description": "Volume consumed by one unit of product $$p$$"
  },
  "production_capacity": {
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "entry": "$$K_t$$",
    "description": "Combined production capacity in period $$t$$"
  },
  "own_warehouse_capacity": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "entry": "$$W$$",
    "description": "Maximum in-house storage volume"
  },
  "holding_cost_own": {
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "entry": "$$h_t^{\\mathrm{own}}$$",
    "description": "Holding cost per cubic meter for in-house storage in period $$t$$"
  },
  "holding_cost_external": {
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "entry": "$$h_t^{\\mathrm{ext}}$$",
    "description": "Holding cost per cubic meter for external storage in period $$t$$"
  },
  "initial_inventory": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "entry": "$$I_{p,0}$$",
    "description": "Inventory of product $$p$$ at the start of the first planning period"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "entry": "$$x_{p,t}$$",
    "description": "Production quantity of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$"
  },
  "inventory_in_own_warehouse": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "entry": "$$i_{p,t}^{\\mathrm{own}}$$",
    "description": "End-of-period inventory of product $$p$$ stored in the factory warehouse"
  },
  "inventory_in_external_storage": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "entry": "$$i_{p,t}^{\\mathrm{ext}}$$",
    "description": "End-of-period inventory of product $$p$$ stored in external warehouse space"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "shape": "scalar",
    "entry": "$$\\mathrm{TC}$$",
    "description": "Minimum total production and storage cost"
  }
}

